          "term": "net.ipv4.tcp_slow_start_after_idle = 1   # Linux default",
          "h": "Idle reuse doesn't save slow start",
          "b": "Linux resets the congestion window after a connection sits idle. A pooled connection that was idle still skips both handshakes, but a large response on it ramps up again. Connections in steady use keep their larger window."
        },
        {
          "clock": "fix",
          "badge": "busy pooled connection: 1 RTT = 100 ms",
